9494	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s10","entry":{"id":"review-e37bea766dda56bafcb340f70ecbc8ee","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T13:29:54.392Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Keeping old paths unchanged and the scan in report mode satisfies upstream ac5.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md says the ordering reversal is decided, but explicitly calls the ac5/ac6 transfer a 'Consequence still to be settled with the user'. It describes existing ac5 as deleting the wrappers and running the scan in failing mode. The LLD silently replaces that criterion with its opposite. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Obtain and record the upstream criterion amendment before claiming coverage; distinguish the approved ordering decision from the unresolved scope transfer.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"ghAuthOk currently returns boolean.","evidence":"github.ts declares `ghAuthOk(): { readonly ok: true } | { readonly ok: false; readonly reason: string }`. tracker-auto.ts consumes `auth.ok` and `auth.reason`. A boolean replacement breaks this existing contract. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts]","action":"Specify and preserve the discriminated result, including its failure reason.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The terminal approval service currently runs tracker push, check-in and attachment publication locally.","evidence":"The full approve body calls `approveArtifactByJsonPath`, `syncPlanTasks`, the workflow-specific autoPush function, `commitApprovedArtifacts`, and `attachApprovedDocuments`. Both publication helpers call commitAndPushArtifacts. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts]","action":"Preserve this ordering and its configuration gates when moving the operation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Existing git_diff supports the proposed cached, quiet commit-detection operation.","evidence":"gitDiffTool accepts `staged`, but no `cached` or `quiet` fields; its input schema sets `additionalProperties: false`. Its implementation executes a normal diff and numstat, treating nonzero diff exit as failure. It does not expose the old quiet-exit-status contract. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/diff.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Specify a concrete supported mapping using the typed staged-diff result, or identify a separately owned tool extension. Define how staged changes are detected without interpreting a tool failure as changes.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The new daemon method parameters preserve the existing client operations.","evidence":"The existing sync signature is `sync(repoPath: string, epicHash: string)`. teamRefresh accepts `branch?: string`; teamClaim and teamRelease require `unit: Omit<UnitRef, 'repoPath'>`. The LLD specifies only repo for these methods. trackerSetup also accepts options but has no destination daemon method specified. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/cli/services/team.ts]","action":"Define complete request and response shapes, including epicHash, unit identity, branch and setup options; name the daemon method for trackerSetup.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The asynchronous conversion inventory covers all affected callers.","evidence":"services/index.ts declares synchronous sync, teamClaim and teamRelease results. command.ts reads `r.status` immediately after sync and directly returns claim/release strings. team/gate.ts synchronously calls `readAssignee`, `addAssignee`, and `setAssignee`. These concrete conversion sites are absent from the stated TrackerPort inventory and migration tasks. [files: src/cli/services/index.ts, src/cli/command.ts, src/workflow/team/gate.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"Inventory and design the full async propagation through team gates, service interfaces, command consumers and their callers, including IssueOps and LoadTracker where affected.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Preserving CommitArtifactsResult alone preserves approval result compatibility.","evidence":"The client returns ApproveOutcome with separate `approval`, `tracker`, `tasks`, `commit`, `attach`, and `attachCommit` fields, and accepts `withTracker`. The daemon returns WorkflowApproveResult; FollowOnOutcome.kind currently permits only 'bugfix-advance', 'bugfix-complete', 'tracker-attach', and 'tasks-sync'. The LLD adds results without defining their discriminants, payloads, adaptation, or withTracker behavior. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts, src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts]","action":"Define the additive followOn union and payloads, client result adaptation, and preservation of withTracker=false. Document compatibility for batch and single-artifact callers.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Moving terminal team operations to daemon methods is consistent with the approved s10-before-s9 boundary.","evidence":"The plan explicitly decides 's10 lands first' and explains that refreshPolicy needs a daemon method because tools.call executes only one registry tool. team.ts currently imports and invokes refreshPolicy locally. The proposed whole-operation daemon boundary addresses that dependency. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, src/cli/services/team.ts]","action":"Retain this ownership boundary. The prose adequately identifies the client-to-daemon direction and daemon ownership; a component diagram is optional. Complete the missing method contracts identified above.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Repeating approve after a failed push completes publication using the unchanged commit-and-push behavior.","evidence":"commitAndPushArtifacts returns immediately when nothing is staged: `reason: 'nothing to commit (already up to date)'`. Push runs only after a new commit. After a successful local commit and rejected or denied push, an unchanged retry therefore never retries that push. The LLD promises both this behavior and recovery on repeat approve. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts]","action":"Design explicit retry of pending publication independently of staged changes, with a defined durable or derivable recovery state.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"A denied commit-and-push step can always report committed=false while preserving the old result semantics.","evidence":"The old function returns `{ committed: true, pushed: false }` when push fails after commit. Section 4 instead says denial goes into reason 'with committed false', including a denial at push. This loses an already completed side effect and misinforms recovery. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Define phase-specific outcomes: preserve committed=true after a successful commit, report the failed phase, and stop subsequent calls. Include denial at push explicitly.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The acceptance mapping proves the proposed preservation and recovery behavior.","evidence":"The proposed tests cover repeated tracker creation and denial stopping, but omit failed-push recovery after a successful local commit, withTracker=false, propagation of epicHash/unit/branch/setup options, and command consumption of asynchronous results. The existing commit helper and synchronous command consumers expose failures those tests would miss. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/cli/services/team.ts, src/cli/command.ts]","action":"Add explicit tests for these contracts and recovery cases, including a real local commit followed by denied push and a retry with no new staged changes. Test trackerSetup through its specified daemon endpoint.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":6,"med":3,"low":2,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T13:29:54.392Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
