566	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s10","entry":{"id":"98b2a3776b1542979d2234a5e5778ddd","actor":{"id":"insrc:design.story","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T13:32:51.396Z","operation":"update","revision":{"number":2,"contentHash":"5c427bdf679b67784328ebb6d28b6b00721b776ea1f9b2e5a774b87286f4a032"},"outcome":{"result":"ok","summary":"Applied daemon review round 1 (6 HIGH, 3 MED): ghAuthOk result shape, staged diff mapping, daemon method shapes, async inventory, phase-specific commit/push outcomes, followOn union, tests."},"addresses":[]}}
10632	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s10","entry":{"id":"review-1ce2e21f3e6df310ee420da9e08144dc","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T13:32:53.298Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The LLD supplies the complete replacement table required to preserve every wrapper's contract.","evidence":"DEF s10 ac1 requires a replacement table mapping every github.ts wrapper. The LLD names tool families but explicitly leaves 'the exact tool or op for each of the 38 wrappers' to tasks. Actual wrappers have materially different contracts: ghCreateLabel returns false on error, ghCreateProject returns null, while runGh throws GhCommandError. The blanket statement that a gh wrapper throws does not specify these mappings. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Complete the wrapper-to-definition/input/output/failure table in the LLD, including nullable and best-effort wrappers, before implementation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Keeping check-in commits enabled when withTracker=false preserves current client behavior.","evidence":"approve executes 'if (!withTracker) return { approval, ...(tasks !== undefined ? { tasks } : {}) };' before commitApprovedArtifacts and attachApprovedDocuments. The proposed behavior would commit and push files for a flag that currently prevents those operations. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts]","action":"Preserve the early-return semantics, or obtain an explicit upstream decision authorizing the changed commit/push behavior and update compatibility and tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing commit helper reports a successful local commit separately from a failed push.","evidence":"commitAndPushArtifacts catches push failure after git commit and returns '{ committed: true, pushed: false, reason: `committed locally; push failed: ...` }'. Its earlier empty-index branch returns 'nothing to commit (already up to date)' without pushing. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Retain these phase-specific results and the explicit non-retry policy.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing typed callTool helper supports checked registry calls and structured failures.","evidence":"callTool accepts '(tool: T, input: Static<T[\"inputSchema\"]>, deps: ToolDeps)' and returns TypedToolResult. It verifies registry definition identity, calls executeTool, and rejects absent typed data with 'schema-mismatch'. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"Use concrete tool definitions and supply the complete ToolDeps context; caller identity alone is not the helper's argument contract.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Adding tracker auto-push while leaving the existing tasks-sync follow-on unchanged yields one correctly gated tracker push.","evidence":"followOnTasksSync already calls 'const push = autoPushTasksOnPlan(path)' after syncPlanTasks. handler-runtime invokes it unconditionally for approved plans. Adding the proposed tracker-push step without restructuring this existing seam duplicates the push path and leaves a tracker push active when withTracker=false. [files: src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts]","action":"Specify one ordered approval pipeline, split task reconciliation from publication, and apply withTracker and stop-on-denial rules to every publication path.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The async TrackerPort migration is sufficiently specified by the listed claim/release callers and a later IssueOps/LoadTracker search.","evidence":"teamContext synchronously calls whoAmI; teamGate and readHolder synchronously consume port results. approval-gate defines 'type Decide = (...) => GateOutcome' and invokes teamGate through authorizeStageChange. author-gate exposes synchronous assertMayAuthor/assertMayBuild and consumes readHolder; handoff also consumes these gates. These authorization contracts are absent from the proposed async signatures and explicit caller inventory. The analyzer also reported incomplete graph coverage, so it cannot establish completeness. [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/team/gate.ts, src/workflow/team/approval-gate.ts, src/workflow/team/author-gate.ts, src/workflow/team/handoff.ts]","action":"Trace and specify the async propagation through authorization, authoring, build, review-fix and handoff entry points, including their callers and test seams; coordinate the overlapping s9 changes.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The specified followOn additions contain enough information to reconstruct the unchanged ApproveOutcome.","evidence":"ApproveOutcome.tasks is the full TaskSyncResult, and attach can be AttachUnitResult, including an error or skipped reason. Existing FollowOnOutcome.tasks contains only created/changed/withdrawn/added arrays; followOnTasksSync collapses close failures into a note. Existing tracker-attach is BUILD-only, while the client attaches design.epic/design.story/plan documents. The three proposed new kinds carry only AutoPushResult and two CommitArtifactsResults, leaving the full tasks and document-attachment results unspecified. [files: src/workflow/gates.ts, src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts, src/daemon/tracker-attach.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts]","action":"Define lossless typed payloads for task reconciliation and document attachment, including skipped/error outcomes, and show the exact daemon-to-ApproveOutcome adapter.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Keeping the legacy wrappers unchanged and leaving the scan in report mode is authorized scope for s10.","evidence":"Current DEF s10 ac5 explicitly requires the old paths to 'remain in place and unchanged' and the scan to stay in report mode. docs/plans/tool-registry.md records the approved revision-6 decision transferring deletion and final inventory regeneration to s9. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Retain this boundary and update the stale adjacent-scope summaries that still attribute final removal to s7.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed process relationship changes require a separate ERD or UX mock to be understandable.","evidence":"No separate ERD or UX mock is necessary here: the LLD's method contracts identify CLI-to-daemon direction, one request per operation, daemon ownership and compatibility behavior. This is an execution-boundary change rather than a new persistent entity relationship or changed UI layout. No linked s10 companion rendering is asserted as verified. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S010/LLD.md, src/cli/services/team.ts, src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts]","action":"Keep the prose contracts; an optional sequence diagram could clarify the corrected approval ordering. Interpret this finding as adequacy of the supplied prose, not a requirement for additional visuals.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Stopping at a denial before git_commit guarantees that nothing remains staged.","evidence":"git_stage executes 'git add ... -- ...paths' before git_commit receives its separate approval. If staging succeeds and commit approval is denied, the proposed stop-at-first-failure sequence performs no restoration. stage.ts explicitly reports the resulting indexAfter. Thus the postcondition 'nothing is staged after a denial before the commit' is false. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/stage.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Either document that already-approved staging remains, or design safe restoration preserving the pre-existing index. Add a denial-after-stage test that checks actual index contents.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The acceptance mapping covers the important behavioral cases introduced by this migration.","evidence":"The LLD maps all six criterion IDs, but its tests omit several explicitly promised paths: client disconnect during follow-ons, older-daemon method-not-found, and complete preservation of tasks/attachment error results. Its withTracker=false test checks only absence of tracker publication while encoding changed commit behavior. Actual code also contains the existing task-publication seam and synchronous authorization contracts that need regression coverage. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S010/LLD.md, src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts, src/workflow/team/approval-gate.ts, src/shared/ipc-client.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts]","action":"Add targeted cases for disconnect and old-daemon failures, one publication per plan approval, lossless outcome adaptation, async authorization, and the corrected withTracker/index-denial semantics.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":5,"med":2,"low":4,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T13:32:53.298Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
