590	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s10","entry":{"id":"f4b6863f0ead45b5873b86e7fac0db74","actor":{"id":"insrc:design.story","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T13:38:56.367Z","operation":"update","revision":{"number":3,"contentHash":"61fd6d5d13a1fb047d4ed4a934cc9e1c1d00a18f473285daf832d6e6648a2a13"},"outcome":{"result":"ok","summary":"Applied daemon review round 2 (5 HIGH, 2 MED): withTracker semantics, one ordered approve pipeline, lossless followOn adapter, full async propagation inventory, staged-index outcome, full replacement table, tests."},"addresses":[]}}
442	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s10","entry":{"id":"832bef2716c540bfac5a2421ee215973","actor":{"id":"insrc:design.story","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T13:39:05.465Z","operation":"update","revision":{"number":4,"contentHash":"2747822651172012545fa1e7995819a9fdeaef5f69b26bac72e42610729c068a"},"outcome":{"result":"ok","summary":"Consistency: withTracker false keeps the early return everywhere."},"addresses":[]}}
9684	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s10","entry":{"id":"review-6202e403afd12c68c76785a0c3b93bb7","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T13:39:13.157Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The replacement table covers every tracker operation required by s10 ac1.","evidence":"DEF §6.10 requires each github.ts caller to move through the registry. github-adapter.ts also directly invokes runGh for assignee reads/edits and PR list/create/view. The design supplies no replacement rows or result mappings for these operations; enumerating the named gh wrappers does not cover them. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"Add explicit mappings for assignee operations and signoff PR operations, including their validation, rereads and failure semantics.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Approval currently runs tracker publication and both artifact commits in the terminal client, while daemon approval runs bugfix, Task sync and BUILD attachment follow-ons.","evidence":"Client approve() calls syncPlanTasks, autoPush*, commitApprovedArtifacts and attachApprovedDocuments. handler-runtime.ts composes advanceApprovedBugfixes, followOnTasksSync and followOnTrackerAttach; followOnTasksSync currently calls autoPushTasksOnPlan. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts]","action":"Preserve the proposed removal of duplicate plan publication when consolidating these paths.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed commit sequence preserves all existing no-op results.","evidence":"The old implementation filters paths with existsSync and returns 'no artifact files on disk' when none remain. §2.2 specifies rev-parse → stage → diff → commit → push without that filtering branch. git_stage rejects an empty paths array, and staging missing paths fails instead of preserving the old result. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/stage.ts]","action":"Specify existence filtering before staging, preserve the no-files reason, and test mixed existing/missing paths and all-missing paths.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"callTool and git_stage provide the typed execution and post-staging result needed by the proposed facade.","evidence":"callTool accepts a TypedTool definition, schema-derived input and ToolDeps, returning success/data or error. gitStageTool is a TypedTool and returns paths and indexAfter, with warnings if its post-mutation index read fails. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/stage.ts]","action":"Pass actual tool definitions and ToolDeps; retain index-listing warnings rather than claiming indexAfter is always authoritative.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The async propagation inventory identifies the consumers that need deliberate changes.","evidence":"tasks-sync.ts builds a synchronous CloseIssue callback: 'const r = gate.port.issueOps.close(issue); return r.ok ...'. github-adapter.ts loadTracker synchronously reads tracker.whoAmI(), and createIssue reads issueOps.create/linkSubIssue synchronously. These concrete consumers are not resolved in the propagation contract. A compiler sweep helps, but does not specify the callback contract or async loader propagation. [files: src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"Include IssueOps, CloseIssue, loadTracker and their callers explicitly, stating which callback contracts become asynchronous and where denial must escape.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed relationship and interaction documentation is sufficient without additional diagrams.","evidence":"The design names client→daemon methods and parameter/result contracts, the shared registry facade, and an ordered per-artifact approval pipeline. This changes execution ownership rather than persisted entity relationships; the prose adequately describes those boundaries. No companion rendering is claimed or required for these contracts. [files: src/cli/services/team.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts]","action":"Keep these contracts synchronized when correcting the missing operation mappings.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"An older daemon will reject the extended workflow.approve request with method-not-found.","evidence":"workflow.approve already exists. handleWorkflowApprove reads known fields from params and ignores withTracker; its follow-on callback still runs followOnTasksSync, including publication. A new client sending withTracker:false to this daemon receives an ordinary response after side effects, rather than the promised incompatibility error. [files: src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts]","action":"Require a capability/version check before invoking extended approval, or introduce a versioned method. Test against the existing handler that accepts the method but ignores the new field.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Keeping the legacy wrappers unchanged and landing s10 before s9 follows the approved scope transfer.","evidence":"DEF s10 ac5 requires old paths to remain unchanged. docs/plans/tool-registry.md §'s10 lands before s9' records approved DEF revision 6 and transfers deletion and failing-scan criteria to s9. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Retain this ordering and avoid implementing s9's deletion criteria in s10.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Approval denial is represented as a rejected tool failure with the stated denial reasons.","evidence":"executor.ts returns failed('denied', ..., denial), not rejected, for approval refusal. The actual timeout reason is 'timed-out'. The design's detection text says 'kind is rejected' and elsewhere names 'expired', while also treating rejected as a swallowable gh failure. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts]","action":"Use ToolFailure.kind === 'denied' and its typed denial field, including cancellation and timed-out. Keep ordinary rejected command failures separate throughout facade and adapter catches.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"tracker.sync can complete missing tracker publication after a disconnected approval.","evidence":"syncTracker explicitly states 'Read-only against GitHub; never edits issues.' It reads issue state/labels and patches local tracker metadata. When no Epic issue exists it returns 'Epic not pushed yet'. The proposed tracker.sync runs this same function, so it cannot create the missing issues promised by the recovery path. [files: src/workflow/tracker/sync.ts, src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts]","action":"Name an actual publication retry operation, or design publication recovery explicitly; do not advertise tracker.sync as repairing missing tracker records.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The test strategy provides explicit coverage for all six upstream acceptance criteria.","evidence":"The design maps ac1–ac6 to facade equivalence, RPC-only client services, tracker equivalence, denial stopping, unchanged legacy exports and complete migration inventory tests. These correspond to DEF §6.10. They are proposed tests, not existing or executed verification. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S010/LLD.md]","action":"Extend the mapped cases for missing-path filtering, direct runGh operations, actual denied failure values and an older daemon that already implements workflow.approve. Correct the test description saying three additive kinds to four.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":5,"med":1,"low":5,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T13:39:13.157Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
