421	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s10","entry":{"id":"cdb83ce2980d47ad990703ba90f641bc","actor":{"id":"insrc:design.story","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T14:00:17.959Z","operation":"update","revision":{"number":6,"contentHash":"995debbfc2594d313a3c282e0e0abed6a3a7064dd73247d02e01d4013031c1e9"},"outcome":{"result":"ok","summary":"Consistency: method name and denial reasons."},"addresses":[]}}
10692	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s10","entry":{"id":"review-2e0683c83ef5dde667dcf0874cfc6cf1","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T14:00:21.009Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The design provides a complete migration mapping for terminal-client git and gh operations required by s10 ac2 and ac6.","evidence":"DEF revision 6 includes 'any other service a complete search finds that runs git or gh'. src/cli/services/maintenance.ts performs git rev-parse, fetch, checkout and merge through capture/stream, whose implementations spawn processes. The LLD explicitly says maintenance was not read and supplies no operation contract or replacement row for it. Deferring this known scope to task-time discovery leaves the design incomplete. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json, src/cli/services/maintenance.ts]","action":"Read the remaining services and include concrete migration rows, daemon contracts and tests for each discovered operation, including maintenance.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The terminal approval flow currently performs approval, plan reconciliation, publication, artifact commit and attachment locally.","evidence":"approve() calls approveArtifactByJsonPath, awaits syncPlanTasks for plans, returns early for !withTracker, then calls autoPush*, commitApprovedArtifacts and attachApprovedDocuments. The latter can perform a second commitAndPushArtifacts call. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts]","action":"Preserve these result payloads when moving the operation behind IPC.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"tracker.sync is read-only against GitHub and cannot repair missing publication.","evidence":"syncTracker reads unit bindings, calls ghAuthOk and ghGetIssueState, and writes local tracker metadata with patchTrackerMeta. With no Epic binding it returns 'Epic not pushed yet (its head is not bound to an issue)'. It performs no GitHub write. [files: src/workflow/tracker/sync.ts]","action":"Retain the distinction between synchronization and publication.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed gh_pr_view reuse supplies all fields needed by readSignoffState without a known prerequisite change.","evidence":"gh_pr_view accepts only cwd, repo and number, with additionalProperties:false. Its fixed PR_VIEW_FIELDS omits mergedAt, reviewDecision and reviews. Existing readSignoffState reads reviewDecision and, when since is supplied, reviews to detect changes requested. The LLD's 'Known now: none' gap statement is false; the proposed reuse cannot preserve those decisions. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/pr.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"Record and resolve the s5 back-flow for the necessary PR fields before implementation. Specify the resulting input/output contract and test both review-state paths.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"ghAddProjectItem maps to an existing tool named gh_project_item_add.","evidence":"The implementation declares id: 'gh:project:item-add'. The existing closed mapping test also maps ghAddProjectItem to 'gh:project:item-add'. callTool rejects an unregistered definition rather than executing it. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/project.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/gh-tracker-mapped-ops.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts]","action":"Use the existing ghProjectItemAddTool definition and correct the replacement-table ID.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The approval RPC has one consistent contract across the design, migration and client tests.","evidence":"Section 2.5 and migration step 4 extend workflow.approve, while the error paths, state-after and versioning test require workflow.approvePipeline exclusively. The current handler registers workflow.approve, and handleWorkflowApprove casts parameters without reading withTracker. Following the extension contract permits an older daemon to accept the request while ignoring the requested early return. [files: src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts]","action":"Choose one versioned RPC contract, define its full parameters and registration, and make all sections and tests agree. Preserve the explicit failure against older daemons.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Compiler-driven propagation alone detects every missing await after TrackerPort becomes asynchronous.","evidence":"IssueOps.ensureMilestone currently returns void, and createIssueOps implements it by calling ghEnsureMilestone. A caller can discard a Promise<void> without a TypeScript error. The same applies to other calls whose results are ignored, so 'fix every type error until none remain' cannot establish complete awaiting. [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"Keep the compiler sweep, but add a semantic no-floating-promises check or explicit runtime sequence assertions for discarded-result calls and callbacks.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed follow-on payload additions can preserve the existing response fields without a stored-data migration.","evidence":"FollowOnOutcome currently contains kind, artifactPath, ok, note, tasks and attach; WorkflowApproveResult carries it as an optional response field. ApproveOutcome separately exposes tasks, tracker, commit, attach and attachCommit. Adding distinct optional payload fields while retaining tasks and attach supports the stated adapter without changing these stored artifact shapes. [files: src/workflow/gates.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts]","action":"Retain existing fields as specified and verify the lossless adapter. The prose adequately identifies payload ownership and direction; an ERD is unnecessary for these response-only additions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Keeping the old wrappers unchanged and leaving the spawn scan in report mode matches the approved s10/s9 scope transfer.","evidence":"DEF revision 6 s10 ac5 says the old paths 'remain in place and unchanged' and the scan stays in report mode. docs/plans/tool-registry.md records 's10 lands first' and moves deletion and the failing scan to s9. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Follow the revision 6 boundary; update stale adjacent-scope descriptions that still assign deletion to s7.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Every denial in the signoff adapter escapes and fails the calling stage.","evidence":"The LLD explicitly preserves logging rather than returning a failure for the signoff link comment. openSignoffRequest currently catches every error from ghPostCommentReturningId, logs 'the signoff request was opened but not linked from its issue', and returns success. Keeping that handling swallows ToolDenied before attempt() can rethrow it, contradicting ac4 and the blanket denial rule. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts, .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json]","action":"Specify that the inner catch rethrows ToolDenied while retaining best-effort logging for ordinary gh failures; test denial after PR creation and reuse on retry.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The replacement-table failure mapping covers the actual shared ToolFailure variants.","evidence":"ToolFailureKind includes 'timed-out', 'conversion-failed' and 'schema-mismatch' in addition to the four gh failure kinds and 'denied'. The LLD discusses schema failure separately but gives no mapping for conversion-failed or non-approval timed-out. callTool returns these failures directly; the old GhCommandError/PortFailureKind union cannot carry all of them unchanged. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"Define explicit handling for every ToolFailureKind, distinguishing command timeout from approval timeout and ensuring conversion/schema failures cannot become best-effort success.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of the six current upstream acceptance criteria has a proposed proving-test mapping.","evidence":"The approved DEF has s10 ac1–ac6. The LLD maps them respectively to replacement/result tests, IPC service tests, legacy-equivalence tests, denial tests, unchanged-old-path tests and site-list/migration-record tests. These are proposed tests, not evidence that implementation already passes. The approval tests must be reconciled with the conflicting RPC contract identified above. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/gh-tracker-mapped-ops.test.ts, src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/tracker.test.ts]","action":"Retain the six-way mapping, add the discovered maintenance and signoff-denial cases, and resolve the RPC naming before building.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":4,"med":3,"low":5,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T14:00:21.009Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
