8678	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s10","entry":{"id":"review-d252db5821ac833325f53ae023d85352","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T14:04:04.835Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers the revised s10 scope while preserving old wrappers for s9.","evidence":"The current DEF's s10 ac1–ac6 require registry migration, daemon execution of client operations, compatibility, denial propagation, unchanged legacy paths and site coverage. docs/plans/tool-registry.md explicitly records: 's10 lands first' and 's10 keeps the old paths unchanged (its ac5)'. The design addresses those requirements. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Retain the revised scope and sequencing.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Client approval currently runs publication, artifact commit and document attachment locally, while daemon approval runs the existing follow-ons.","evidence":"approve() directly invokes approveArtifactByJsonPath, syncPlanTasks, autoPush*, commitApprovedArtifacts and attachApprovedDocuments. The workflow.approve handler composes advanceApprovedBugfixes, followOnTasksSync and followOnTrackerAttach; followOnTasksSync currently calls autoPushTasksOnPlan. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts]","action":"Preserve the proposed removal of the duplicate plan publication when moving the pipeline.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The legacy commit helper leaves a completed commit local after push failure and does not retry that push on a subsequent call with nothing staged.","evidence":"commitAndPushArtifacts returns 'committed locally; push failed: ...' with committed:true after a failed push. Its earlier staged-diff check returns 'nothing to commit (already up to date)' before reaching push on a repeat call. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Keep the phase-specific result mapping and repeat-call tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The typed call helper exists, and gh_pr_view needs an extension for signoff review fields.","evidence":"callTool accepts a TypedTool definition, typed input and ToolDeps, returning success/data or error:ToolFailure. ghPrViewTool currently accepts only cwd, repo and number, and PR_VIEW_FIELDS omits mergedAt, reviewDecision and reviews. readSignoffState explicitly requests those fields through runGh today. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/pr.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"Implement and validate the stated additive gh_pr_view extension; pass caller through ToolDeps.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The async propagation inventory includes all callback contracts needed by tracker publication.","evidence":"The inventory omits src/workflow/tracker/unit-issue.ts. ExtraStep.run is declared '() => PortResult<void>', ExtrasDeps.comments is synchronous, and runUnitExtras reads 'const r = step.run()' without awaiting it. tracker-auto supplies IssueOps callbacks and a port.listComments loader to these contracts. Making IssueOps asynchronous therefore also requires changing this runner, its callback contracts and its callers; the listed CloseIssue and LoadTracker changes do not cover them. [files: src/workflow/tracker/unit-issue.ts, src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts, src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/unit-extras.test.ts]","action":"Explicitly add ExtraStep.run, ExtrasDeps.comments, commentsOnce, runUnitExtras and all publication callers/tests to the async migration, preserving sequential execution and comment reconciliation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The follow-on expansion can preserve existing result fields without rewriting stored artifacts.","evidence":"FollowOnOutcome currently carries kind, artifactPath, ok, note, tasks and attach. ApproveOutcome separately carries approval, tracker, commit, tasks, attach and attachCommit. The proposed additions retain those existing fields and explicitly map the richer task, attachment and commit results back to the client shape. These are operation-result contracts rather than a replacement artifact storage model. [files: src/workflow/gates.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts]","action":"Keep existing tasks and attach payloads alongside the additions, and verify the proposed lossless adapter tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design documents the relevant process relationships sufficiently without requiring an ERD or UX mock.","evidence":"The current client imports team gate and policy-refresh implementations directly; existing teamPark/teamResume already use RPC. The design specifies client-to-daemon operation endpoints, daemon ownership, ordered registry execution and older-daemon behavior. This changes execution boundaries rather than persistent entity relationships or UI layout. No generated visual companion is claimed in the supplied design. [files: src/cli/services/team.ts, src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"The prose contracts suffice. A component or sequence diagram would be optional; reconcile the stale alternative text saying team init moves with §3.5, which keeps its starter-policy write local.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Rethrowing ToolDenied from registry rows and the adapter is sufficient to ensure a denied tracker extra stops the stage.","evidence":"tracker-auto's guarded() catches every exception and returns '{ ok: false, ... kind: rejected }'. runUnitExtras records a failed step and executes 'continue', allowing later extras to run. pushEpic/pushStory then return created/already-exists with extrasFailed. Thus an awaited ToolDenied can still become a nonterminal extra failure, contradicting ac4 despite the design's explicit adapter-level rethrow. [files: src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts, src/workflow/tracker/unit-issue.ts, .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json]","action":"Specify ToolDenied rethrows through guarded() and the extras runner, stop subsequent extras, and ensure publication/pipeline failure retains the denial and already-created object identities. Add a denial test at a milestone or comment extra with later calls forbidden.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each revised acceptance criterion has a proposed test mapping.","evidence":"The current DEF has six s10 criteria. The design maps ac1 to wrapper/commit compatibility, ac2 to RPC and pipeline contracts, ac3 to recorded behavior and async gates, ac4 to denial variants, ac5 to unchanged legacy paths/report mode, and ac6 to site inventory coverage. These are proposed tests, as the design explicitly acknowledges. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S010/LLD.md, src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/unit-extras.test.ts]","action":"Retain all six mappings and extend ac3/ac4 coverage to the omitted extras callback contracts and denial propagation identified above. Correct the test description saying 'three additive follow-on kinds' to four.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":2,"med":0,"low":7,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T14:04:04.835Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
