11113	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s10","entry":{"id":"review-fc86b28866fd356feaaf722122e7d548","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T14:07:08.598Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design addresses s10's six upstream acceptance criteria, including retaining the legacy paths until s9.","evidence":"DEF §6.10 requires registry migration, daemon-only client operations, preserved tracker results, denial propagation, unchanged legacy paths and a complete migration inventory. The design supplies corresponding contracts, migration steps and acceptance mappings. docs/plans/tool-registry.md explicitly records: 's10 keeps the old paths unchanged (its ac5)'. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Keep the DEF revision 6 scope as the implementation baseline.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The terminal currently performs approval, publication, check-in and document attachment locally, whereas daemon approval runs the existing follow-ons.","evidence":"The complete approve() body calls approveArtifactByJsonPath, syncPlanTasks, autoPush*, commitApprovedArtifacts and attachApprovedDocuments. handler-runtime.ts wires advanceApprovedBugfixes, followOnTasksSync and followOnTrackerAttach into workflow.approve. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts]","action":"Preserve the explicitly documented ordering when moving these operations.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A repeated commit-and-push does not retry an earlier failed push when the index is empty.","evidence":"commitAndPushArtifacts returns 'nothing to commit (already up to date)' immediately after an empty cached diff, before reaching git push. Its push catch returns committed:true and pushed:false. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Retain the documented user-push recovery and its regression test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing gh_pr_view lacks the signoff review fields and requires the proposed additive extension.","evidence":"pr.ts defines PR_VIEW_FIELDS as PR_JSON_FIELDS + ',body,mergeable,mergeStateStatus'; neither list includes mergedAt, reviewDecision or reviews. Its input accepts only cwd, repo and number. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/pr.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/schemas.ts]","action":"Extend both field selection and checked output shape while preserving default rendering and results.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The typed staged-diff result supports detecting changes without interpreting a failed command as a nonempty diff.","evidence":"gitDiffTool accepts staged:true, returns structured files, diffBytes and truncated, and explicitly fails unsuccessful diff or numstat commands. This supports the design's distinction between an empty successful result and failure. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/diff.ts]","action":"Define the emptiness predicate using the complete structured file list rather than captured body length.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The stated catch-all inventory is sufficient to make a denial inside Task reconciliation escape as ToolDenied.","evidence":"syncPlanTasks wraps openTracker and the awaited sets.syncOnPlanApproval in 'catch (err) { return { error: err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err) }; }'. The design enumerates denial-rethrow sites but omits this catch, while asserting that denial escapes through CloseIssue. Awaiting the callback alone still converts that denial into an ordinary error result here. [files: src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts, src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts]","action":"Explicitly change syncPlanTasks to rethrow ToolDenied, and define the tasks-sync pipeline boundary that records it and stops publication and later steps. Test denial during a withdrawn-Task close through the real syncPlanTasks wrapper.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The existing adapter attempt() wraps only GhCommandError.","evidence":"attempt() catches every thrown value and calls failure(err). failure() handles GhCommandError specially but converts every other exception to kind:'rejected'. The design describes it as 'it only wraps GhCommandError'. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"Correct the current-behaviour statement and specify the async attempt implementation explicitly: await the callback inside try, rethrow ToolDenied, and preserve the existing conversion of other exceptions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding richer follow-on payloads can preserve the existing client approval result without rewriting stored tracker data.","evidence":"ApproveOutcome already carries tasks, tracker, commit, attach and attachCommit. FollowOnOutcome currently exposes only a reduced tasks summary, while followOnTasksSync has the full sync result before constructing that summary. The proposed taskSync field and adapter preserve information currently available to the local client. These are response-contract additions, not changes to the stored bindings. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts, src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts]","action":"Retain the lossless adapter tests, including closeFailed and attachment errors.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The revised s10-before-s9 ordering and legacy-path ownership agree with the recorded upstream decision.","evidence":"The decision document says 's10 lands first' and records DEF revision 6 transferring deletion and failing-scan criteria to s9. The current DEF gives s9 ac7/ac8 and s10 an unchanged-paths ac5. The design follows that settled split. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md]","action":"Update stale adjacent-story descriptions during implementation planning so they do not override this recorded split.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design adequately documents the changed process and operation relationships without requiring an ERD or UX mock.","evidence":"The existing client directly imports workflow operations, while handler-runtime owns daemon RPC handlers and callTool invokes the executor. The design names each client-to-daemon endpoint, its request/result, daemon ownership, per-artifact ordering and old-daemon compatibility. These are execution-boundary changes rather than a new persistent entity relationship or UI layout. No linked visual companion is claimed for s10. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/cli/services/team.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts]","action":"A sequence diagram would be optional clarification; the substantive contract corrections in this review remain necessary.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Plain rpc calls provide the stated detectable failure when the socket closes during a moved operation.","evidence":"The shared rpc implementation installs end/close rejection listeners only inside 'if (timeoutMs !== undefined)'. The proposed services call rpc, but the design supplies no timeout or close-handling change. With the default call, a socket closing before its reply can leave the returned Promise pending indefinitely. [files: src/shared/ipc-client.ts, src/cli/client.ts]","action":"Specify close-aware transport handling for these long-running operations without imposing a deadline that conflicts with approval waits. Add a client-side test asserting rejection on premature socket close, separately from daemon pipeline continuation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The denial carrier and commit/push phase distinction match the existing registry and legacy result contracts.","evidence":"ToolFailure carries kind and an optional denial with declined, timed-out, no-client and cancelled. callTool returns failures rather than throwing them. The legacy commit helper distinguishes pre-commit failures from a failed push after a successful commit using committed:true. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Keep the explicit ToolDenied translation and phase-specific commit results; apply the translation at every enclosing catch boundary.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every upstream acceptance criterion has a proposed proving test.","evidence":"The six criteria in DEF §6.10 each have a corresponding acceptance-mapping row. The proposed tests cover registry rows, daemon-only services, preserved outcomes, denial short-circuiting, retained exports and inventory completeness. Existing code confirms that these target real seams: the injectable tracker executor, approval handler dependencies and client rpc boundary. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts, src/shared/ipc-client.ts]","action":"Implement the proposed tests and add the reconciliation-catch and premature-close cases identified above. Correct the test text saying 'three additive follow-on kinds': §3.4 actually introduces four.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":2,"med":1,"low":10,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T14:07:08.598Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
