10484	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s10","entry":{"id":"review-2556f5ee877b9adae1f29e417c1102f4","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T14:09:23.163Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers the current s10 acceptance criteria, including preserving the legacy paths until s9.","evidence":"DEF s10 ac1–ac6 require registry migration, daemon-only client operations, preserved tracker results, denial propagation, unchanged legacy paths and a complete site inventory. The design addresses each. docs/plans/tool-registry.md explicitly records: “Those two criteria moved to s9 ... s10 keeps the old paths unchanged.” The implementation gaps identified below still need correction. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Retain this scope and address the concrete contract and denial findings below.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The client currently performs publication and commits locally, whereas daemon approval runs bugfix, Task-sync and BUILD attachment follow-ons.","evidence":"The complete client approve body calls approveArtifactByJsonPath, syncPlanTasks, autoPush*, commitApprovedArtifacts and attachApprovedDocuments. handler-runtime.ts wires advanceApprovedBugfixes, followOnTasksSync and followOnTrackerAttach. followOnTasksSync currently calls autoPushTasksOnPlan after reconciliation, confirming the duplicate-publication risk the proposed split addresses. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts]","action":"Preserve the proposed separation of reconciliation from publication.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed closeAware transport option addresses an existing pending-request failure.","evidence":"rpc installs its end/close rejection handlers only inside “if (timeoutMs !== undefined)”. A normal request has an error listener but no end/close rejection, matching the design's description. [files: src/shared/ipc-client.ts]","action":"Implement closeAware with settlement protection and the specified premature-close tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The typed registry helper exists, and gh_pr_view needs an extension to supply signoff review fields.","evidence":"callTool takes a typed tool definition, schema-derived input and ToolDeps, returning success data or ToolFailure. ghPrViewTool currently accepts only cwd, repo and number; PR_VIEW_FIELDS lacks mergedAt, reviewDecision and reviews. github-adapter.ts reads exactly those fields in readSignoffState, including individual reviews for the since path. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/pr.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"Implement and validate the additive field selection and output schema together, preserving the existing default result.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Moving commit-and-push callers onto the replacement helper is sufficient to preserve the required stop-on-denial behavior.","evidence":"The new helper returns denial through CommitArtifactsResult rather than throwing. questions.ts commitAndComment currently ignores commitAndPushArtifacts's result and then proceeds to issueOps.comment. resolve-comment.ts commitRecorded also ignores the result and handleResolveComment returns success. The design names these sites but supplies no result-checking contract or failure propagation through recordResolution, commitRecorded and their callers. Merely awaiting the replacement still continues after a denied commit or reports success. [files: src/workflow/questions.ts, src/workflow/resolve-comment.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Specify the async return and failure contracts for both resolution paths. Inspect the returned commit result, stop subsequent operations on denial, and surface the failed stage while retaining information about resolutions already written.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed daemon/client interaction boundary is adequately described without a mandatory diagram.","evidence":"The existing client approval and team services contain the local operations being moved. The design gives named IPC endpoints, request/result shapes, daemon ownership, per-artifact ordering and compatibility behavior. These are operation-boundary changes rather than new persistent entity relationships; the ordered prose is sufficient to explain them. No companion rendering was verified. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/cli/services/team.ts, src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts, .insrc/artifacts/LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s10.json]","action":"Keep the endpoint and sequence descriptions consistent across §2.5 and migration: explicitly use workflow.approvePipeline for the new client contract and workflow.approve for delegation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed result extensions can preserve existing approval payload fields without rewriting stored tracker records.","evidence":"FollowOnOutcome currently has tasks and attach fields, while WorkflowApproveResult contains approved, skipped, codeReview and optional followOn. The design retains these fields and adds separate taskSync, pushed, attachResult and commit payloads. The client's ApproveOutcome already contains approval, tasks, tracker, commit, attach and attachCommit, matching the proposed adapter targets. syncTracker writes existing tracker metadata rather than introducing a new stored shape. [files: src/workflow/gates.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/workflow/tracker/sync.ts]","action":"Retain the old tasks and attach payloads alongside the new fields, and verify the lossless adapter as proposed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Keeping the self-update outside the registry and retaining old wrappers respects the settled cross-Story boundary.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md calls daemon self-update “the one named exemption” and later records the approved s10-before-s9 decision, transferring wrapper deletion and the failing scan to s9. The design preserves those decisions and assigns signoff's remaining runGit calls to s9. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, src/cli/services/maintenance.ts, src/workflow/team/signoff.ts]","action":"Use the settled decision sections as authoritative when reconciling the older adjacent-scope descriptions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Rethrowing ToolDenied in syncPlanTasks lets a withdrawn-Task close denial reach the approval reconciliation boundary.","evidence":"TaskSets.syncOnPlanApproval itself wraps the awaited reconcile call in a catch and returns “{ error: reason }” for every exception. This catch runs before syncPlanTasks's catch. Consequently, changing only the outer wrapper as specified cannot make ToolDenied escape. The thrown error also does not currently carry the partial reconciliation arrays promised for the failed follow-on. [files: src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts, src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts]","action":"Add denial handling to TaskSets.syncOnPlanApproval and define how partial reconciliation progress reaches the pipeline. Preserve ordinary error conversion, but propagate denial and stop publication and subsequent steps.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The commit helper can preserve the distinction between a completed local commit and a failed push.","evidence":"The existing helper returns “{ committed: true, pushed: false, reason: `committed locally; push failed: ...` }” after a push failure. Its nothing-staged branch returns before push, so a repeat invocation does not retry an unpushed commit. The proposed sequence explicitly preserves both behaviors. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/stage.ts]","action":"Keep the proposed real-repository tests for denied push, staged index retention and repeat invocation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The acceptance mapping provides tests for every upstream s10 criterion.","evidence":"The current DEF has six s10 criteria, ac1–ac6. §5 maps all six to registry-row, daemon/client, behavioral-equivalence, denial, legacy-preservation and inventory tests. Existing tracker tests already exercise commit success, rejected push, nothing staged and missing files, providing concrete legacy expectations. The named new tests are proposals, not verified implementations. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json, .insrc/artifacts/LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s10.json, src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/tracker.test.ts, src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts]","action":"Add explicit resolution-path denial cases and a test through the real TaskSets.syncOnPlanApproval catch, covering the two HIGH findings above.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":2,"med":0,"low":9,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T14:09:23.163Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
