9681	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s10","entry":{"id":"review-134d1c6f5f113c983f983eafb64c0361","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T14:15:25.070Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design addresses the six effective s10 acceptance criteria, including preserving the old paths until s9.","evidence":"DEF revision 6 requires registry migration, daemon-based client operations, preserved tracker results, denial propagation, unchanged old paths, and a tested migration inventory. The design provides a corresponding contract and acceptance-test mapping for ac1–ac6. docs/plans/tool-registry.md explicitly records that deletion and failing-mode scan criteria moved to s9. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Retain the revision 6 scope; correct the implementation gaps identified below.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The client currently performs approval publication and commits locally, while daemon plan approval also publishes through followOnTasksSync.","evidence":"cli/services/workflow.ts approve awaits approveArtifactByJsonPath and syncPlanTasks, then calls autoPush*, commitApprovedArtifacts and attachApprovedDocuments. daemon/tasks-sync.ts followOnTasksSync calls syncPlanTasks followed by autoPushTasksOnPlan. handler-runtime.ts composes that follow-on with bugfix and tracker attachment outcomes. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts]","action":"Preserve the proposed single-publication ordering when moving these operations.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Plain rpc currently lacks premature-close rejection, and tracker sync is read-only against GitHub.","evidence":"shared/ipc-client.ts installs end/close rejection listeners only inside `if (timeoutMs !== undefined)`. tracker/sync.ts reads issue state and labels and writes local tracker metadata; it returns skipped with 'Epic not pushed yet (its head is not bound to an issue)' when unbound and performs no GitHub mutation. [files: src/shared/ipc-client.ts, src/workflow/tracker/sync.ts]","action":"Keep closeAware opt-in and timer-free as proposed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing gh_pr_view requires an extension to support the signoff-state reads.","evidence":"builtins/gh/pr.ts accepts cwd, repo and number only, with additionalProperties false. PR_VIEW_FIELDS omits mergedAt, reviewDecision and reviews. github-adapter.ts readSignoffState explicitly requests `state,mergedAt,reviewDecision` or `state,mergedAt,reviews`. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/pr.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"Implement the declared additive extension, including schema and rendering compatibility for selected-field responses.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The stated denial-propagation inventory covers every catch-all on the affected call paths.","evidence":"team/gate.ts actingUser ends with `catch { return undefined; }`; teamGate, claim and release convert all exceptions into refusal outcomes; reviewFixDecision ends with `catch { return 'report-only'; }`. team/approval-gate.ts reviewFixModeFor also catches to report-only, and authorizeStageChange converts exceptions into ApprovalRefusal. These functions are included in the async propagation but omitted from the explicit denial-rethrow inventory. Merely awaiting their port calls preserves these swallowing paths; a denied review-fix operation can continue as a report-only review. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts, src/workflow/team/approval-gate.ts]","action":"Specify isToolDenied rethrows in these catches and their enclosing callers. Add a sequence test proving a denial stops the review or team stage rather than becoming undefined, a generic refusal, or report-only continuation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"A denied withdrawn-Task close preserves enough durable state for a repeated approval to complete reconciliation.","evidence":"task-set.ts reconcile first applies `withdraw`, then calls closeIssueOf. closeIssueOf writes its `pending-close` log only after closeIssue returns. Under the proposed thrown denial, that log is never written. existingTasks excludes withdrawn heads, while retryCloses retries only when the latest close entry has result `pending-close`. Therefore the next reconciliation can omit the still-open issue permanently. Attaching partial arrays to ToolDenied does not repair this durable-state gap. [files: src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts, src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts]","action":"Design a durable pending-close record before attempting the close, or record pending-close on denial before rethrowing. Preserve the original denial and partial progress. Verify retry after denial closes the withdrawn Task's issue.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Keeping legacy wrappers and leaving scan enforcement to s9 follows the effective Story boundary.","evidence":"DEF revision 6 ac5 says the old paths 'remain in place and unchanged' and the forbidden-spawn scan stays in report mode. docs/plans/tool-registry.md records s10 landing first and moving deletion/enforcement to s9. The proposed migration retains those paths. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Update stale adjacent-scope descriptions that still attribute deletion to s7, so the document consistently reflects the settled boundary.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed interaction boundaries are adequately documented without mandatory additional diagrams.","evidence":"The existing client workflow and team services directly invoke workflow modules; the daemon handler owns follow-on composition. Sections 2.5–2.7 and 3.4 explicitly replace those interactions with one daemon request per operation, define request/result ownership, and order per-artifact follow-ons. No new persistent entity relationship is introduced. The supplied design has no linked companion requiring rendering verification. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/cli/services/team.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts]","action":"A sequence diagram could improve readability, but is optional given the explicit pipeline and transport contracts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed failure mapping explicitly distinguishes command failures, schema failures and approval denials using the existing registry contract.","evidence":"tools/types.ts declares missing-tool, missing-signin, unreachable, timed-out, rejected, conversion-failed, schema-mismatch and denied, with a separate denial field. call-tool.ts returns failures as a discriminated result. executor.ts returns denied for approval failure and schema-mismatch for invalid successful output. The design maps all these kinds and keeps approval timeouts distinct from command timeouts. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Preserve these distinctions through the additional catch sites identified above; do not let generic error conversion erase a denial.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every effective acceptance criterion has an explicit proposed test mapping.","evidence":"Compared with DEF revision 6, the acceptance table covers registry result parity (ac1), daemon-only client operations and version errors (ac2), tracker parity and async sequencing (ac3), denial stops (ac4), unchanged legacy exports/report-mode scan (ac5), and per-site recorded-executor coverage plus migration rows (ac6). These are proposed tests, not evidence that implementation tests already pass. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json, src/workflow/team/gate.ts, src/workflow/team/approval-gate.ts, src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts]","action":"Add regression cases for denial through review-fix fallback catches and durable retry of a withdrawn-Task close after denial. Correct the test description saying 'three additive follow-on kinds': section 3.4 defines four.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":2,"med":0,"low":8,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T14:15:25.070Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
