8979	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s10","entry":{"id":"review-b1670c54322d8f20f7f7ccda699fd1d3","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T14:18:14.758Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design addresses the six current s10 acceptance criteria, including retaining the old paths until s9.","evidence":"DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json defines ac1–ac6 as registry migration, daemon transport, behavior preservation, denial propagation, unchanged legacy paths, and complete site coverage. The design provides contracts and acceptance mappings for each. tool-registry.md records: 'Those two criteria moved to s9 ... s10 keeps the old paths unchanged'. Completeness defects are reported separately below. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Retain alignment with DEF revision 6 while correcting the concrete gaps below.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The terminal approval service currently performs approval, plan reconciliation, publication and two artifact commits locally; daemon approval has separate existing follow-ons.","evidence":"workflow.ts approve() awaits approveArtifactByJsonPath and syncPlanTasks, then calls autoPush*, commitApprovedArtifacts and attachApprovedDocuments. handler-runtime.ts wires advanceApprovedBugfixes, followOnTasksSync and followOnTrackerAttach. tasks-sync.ts currently calls autoPushTasksOnPlan after reconciliation. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts, src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts]","action":"Preserve these distinctions when consolidating publication into one daemon pipeline.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The existing git_ls_files tool provides the error-unmatch form specified for the attachment tracked-file check.","evidence":"gitLsFilesTool accepts cwd, paths, cached, others, ignored and maxBytes; its argv starts ['git', '--literal-pathspecs', 'ls-files', '-z']. It has no error-unmatch input and returns success with {files: []} for an unmatched path. attachDocuments currently relies on 'ls-files --error-unmatch' throwing to refuse an untracked attachment. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/workflow/tracker/attach.ts]","action":"Specify a mapping that checks the returned files for the requested literal path, or resolve an explicit tool extension with its owner. Test an untracked file, including the empty-list success result.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The terminal-client inventory includes every operation that reaches workflow code requiring the daemon registry.","evidence":"workflow.ts reviewArtifact() still invokes reviewArtifactFile in the CLI process; run-artifact.ts calls reviewFixModeFor, which reaches reviewFixDecision and the tracker through team gates. workflow.ts resolveFinding() invokes resolveReviewFinding locally; resolve.ts calls authorizeFindingApply, which reaches teamGate and teamContext, including whoAmI and possible issue creation. These operations have no daemon-method replacement rows. command.ts also consumes resolveFinding synchronously. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/cli/services/index.ts, src/cli/command.ts, src/workflow/review/run-artifact.ts, src/workflow/review/resolve.ts, src/workflow/team/approval-gate.ts, src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"Add daemon transport rows for reviewArtifact and resolveFinding, propagate their asynchronous interfaces and command consumers, and test both with claims enforced. Extend the client scan beyond the currently enumerated operations.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Replacing plain git push with the specified git_push call preserves publication behavior and CommitArtifactsResult semantics.","evidence":"The legacy helper executes ['git', '-C', repoPath, 'push'], allowing Git configuration to select the remote and refspec. gitPushTool instead defaults remote to 'origin', resolves ref to the current branch, and executes 'argv.push(remote, ref)'. The design specifies no configuration-resolution mapping. Repositories using another push remote, a differently named upstream branch, or no configured upstream can therefore publish differently or report a different outcome. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/push.ts]","action":"Design configuration-aware push parity or obtain an explicit behavior-change decision. Resolve any required tool capability with s4, and add regression cases for alternate push remotes, differently named upstream branches and missing upstreams.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Denied withdrawn-Task closes can use the existing pending-close log format for durable retry without rewriting stored records.","evidence":"TaskSets.closeIssueOf already records outcomes named 'closed' or 'pending-close' with issue data. retryCloses scans withdrawn Tasks and retries when their latest close outcome is 'pending-close'. The proposed denial handling writes that existing outcome before rethrowing. [files: src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts]","action":"Keep the existing log shape and verify retry using a newly constructed TaskSets instance reading the persisted log.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Landing s10 before s9 while retaining legacy wrappers follows the settled ownership decision.","evidence":"tool-registry.md explicitly records 's10 lands first' and transfers wrapper deletion and the failing scan to s9. The design follows that decision. Its prose identifies client-to-daemon operation ownership, ordered calls, and additive follow-on payloads; these relationships can be assessed without requiring an ERD. No generated companion is claimed or linked for this design. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/pr.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/schemas.ts]","action":"Keep the s5 gh_pr_view extension explicit as a coordinated shared-contract change, including compatibility of default fields.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed closeAware transport option addresses an existing premature-close hang without imposing an approval deadline.","evidence":"rpc currently installs its end/close rejection listeners only inside 'if (timeoutMs !== undefined)'. Without timeoutMs, a connection ending without a reply has no rejection handler. An independent closeAware option can install those listeners without starting the timer, as the design specifies. [files: src/shared/ipc-client.ts]","action":"Ensure settlement and cleanup use timeoutMs-or-closeAware, and test successful replies followed by close as well as premature end/close.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every current acceptance criterion has an identified proving-test category in the proposed strategy.","evidence":"Compared with the actual DEF, ac1 maps to replacement-row and commit-sequence tests; ac2 to client/handler contracts; ac3 to legacy-result and sequencing tests; ac4 to denial tests; ac5 to unchanged-path checks; ac6 to inventory and recorded-executor coverage. These are proposed tests, not evidence of passing implementation. The omitted client paths and push-configuration cases identified above need corresponding coverage. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json, src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/push.ts]","action":"Extend the mapped tests for the findings above. Preserve the explicit distinction between proposed tests and executed validation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":3,"med":0,"low":6,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T14:18:14.758Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
