9064	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s10","entry":{"id":"review-4a4d06c658ea4958415a570b7ca989aa","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T14:22:05.274Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers s10's six current acceptance criteria, including retaining the old paths until s9.","evidence":"DEF §6.10 requires registry-based replacements, daemon-owned client operations, tracker parity, denial propagation, unchanged old paths and per-site registry tests. The design addresses each. The recorded 2026-10-27 decision explicitly transfers deletion and enforcement to s9. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Retain this scope and correct the denial-propagation omissions reported below.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Approval currently runs tracker publication and both commits in the terminal client, while the daemon's Task-sync follow-on also publishes Task issues.","evidence":"The client approve() calls approveArtifactByJsonPath, syncPlanTasks, autoPush*, commitApprovedArtifacts and attachApprovedDocuments. followOnTasksSync separately calls autoPushTasksOnPlan after reconciliation. handler-runtime registers that follow-on under workflow.approve. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts, src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts]","action":"Preserve the proposed single-publication ordering when moving this flow.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Plain rpc calls can remain pending after a premature socket close because close listeners are installed only with timeoutMs.","evidence":"rpc() installs socket.on('end', closed) and socket.on('close', closed) exclusively inside `if (timeoutMs !== undefined)`. Without that option, only response parsing and socket errors settle the request. [files: src/shared/ipc-client.ts]","action":"Implement closeAware with settlement and listener cleanup equivalent to the timed path, without introducing an approval deadline.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The typed registry helper exists, but git_push and gh_pr_view need the extensions identified by this design.","evidence":"callTool accepts a typed tool definition, schema-derived input and ToolDeps, returning TypedToolResult. git_push currently defaults to origin/current branch and appends both to argv. gh_pr_view accepts only cwd, repo and number; its fixed PR_VIEW_FIELDS omit mergedAt, reviewDecision and reviews. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/push.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/pr.ts]","action":"Keep these extensions explicit and preserve existing tool defaults and result contracts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The async propagation design accounts for the principal callback contracts that a TrackerPort conversion affects.","evidence":"TrackerPort and IssueOps currently return synchronous values, including boolean and void methods. loadTracker immediately consumes whoAmI(). syncPlanTasks constructs a synchronous CloseIssue callback and reads r.ok. TaskSets.closeIssueOf similarly reads closed.ok without awaiting. The proposed Promise changes and explicit discarded-result scan address these actual contracts. [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts, src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts, src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts]","action":"Apply the compiler and floating-Promise checks together; type-checking alone cannot detect discarded Promise<void> results.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A denied withdrawn-Task close needs a durable pending-close entry so reconciliation can retry it.","evidence":"closeIssueOf currently writes its close log only after opts.closeIssue returns. retryCloses retries a withdrawn Task only when its latest close entry has result 'pending-close'. Catching a denial, recording that existing log shape and rethrowing therefore addresses a real durability gap without requiring a new stored schema. [files: src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts]","action":"Keep the specified pending-close regression test, including retry after reconstructing the Task service from disk.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The s10-before-s9 sequencing and retention of old wrappers respect the recorded ownership decision.","evidence":"The decision document states 's10 lands first' and transfers deletion/enforcement criteria to s9. DEF §6.10 ac5 requires the old paths to remain unchanged. The design follows this and explicitly identifies overlapping daemon edits and the s4/s5 tool extensions. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md]","action":"Resolve the identified tool-owner back-flows before build if either owner objects.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The changed process relationships and execution ordering are sufficiently documented in prose without requiring an ERD.","evidence":"The numbered approval pipeline documents direction and ordering from client RPC to daemon-owned operations and registry calls. The replacement table identifies operation endpoints, and the compatibility sections describe additive contracts. No new entity ownership or cardinality is introduced. No companion visual is supplied or linked for this design, so no visual rendering was verified. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S010/LLD.md]","action":"A sequence diagram could improve navigation, but is optional given the explicit pipeline prose.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Every catch-all on the moved TrackerPort paths rethrows ToolDenied so denial cannot become an identity fallback or report-only continuation.","evidence":"The design awaits the loader in identity-service.ts and draft-issues.ts but omits their denial catches. IdentityService.idOf catches tracker exceptions and returns `{ source: 'github', status: 'unavailable', identities: [] }`; its outer catch returns osId(). Between those catches, resolveLearner catches adapter.lookup failures and continues to git/OS identity. ensureDraftIssues catches all exceptions and returns `notReady('the draft', 'rejected', true, ..., [])`. Awaiting the new port calls alone therefore still swallows ToolDenied and permits fallback or advisory handling. [files: src/workflow/identity/identity-service.ts, src/understanding/identity.ts, src/workflow/draft-issues.ts]","action":"Explicitly propagate ToolDenied through both identity-service catches, the resolveLearner provider boundary, and ensureDraftIssues. Coordinate the shared identity boundary with s9 and add end-to-end denial tests proving no fallback identity or later stage action occurs.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each upstream acceptance criterion has a proposed proving test category.","evidence":"The design maps ac1 to replacement-row and commit parity tests; ac2 to RPC-only client and handler tests; ac3 to tracker parity and async sequence tests; ac4 to denial tests; ac5 to unchanged-path/report-mode checks; and ac6 to site inventory and registry-path tests. These correspond to DEF §6.10's six criteria. These are proposed tests, not executed verification. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S010/LLD.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md]","action":"Extend ac4 coverage with the identity and draft-hook denial paths identified above.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":0,"low":9,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T14:22:05.274Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
